<div class="content-card legal-doc">
    <p class="notice success" role="note">
        <strong>Draft notice:</strong> This text is an institutional draft for ACMCL College Inc. review. Specific organizational contact points and retention schedules should be filled in by the institution prior to production deployment.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information Vote Collects</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Account registration data:</strong> Full name, email address, normalized email address, hashed password, assigned role (Student or Admin), optional student year level, administrator-assigned voting group, account creation timestamp, email verification timestamp, and session version.</li>
        <li><strong>Verification, recovery, and invitation records:</strong> SHA-256 hashes of single-use 6-digit email verification codes, password recovery codes, and administrator invitation codes, together with issuance, expiration, attempt count, revocation, and consumption timestamps.</li>
        <li><strong>Election and candidate data:</strong> Election names, Philippine-time voting schedules, status, eligible voting group restrictions, position definitions, candidate names, party or affiliation, platforms, and optional candidate photographs stored in private application storage.</li>
        <li><strong>Ballot and selection records:</strong> Each submitted ballot records the voter's account identifier (<code>UserAccountId</code>), the election identifier, the UTC submission timestamp, and the selected candidate and position identifiers. <strong>Ballots are linked to voter accounts in the database</strong> to prevent duplicate voting; this portal is not an anonymous ballot system.</li>
        <li><strong>Session and security tokens:</strong> Essential cookies used strictly for authentication (<code>ACMCL.Voting.Auth</code>), anti-forgery CSRF validation, and signed ballot-review confirmation tokens.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Why This Data Is Used</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To confirm control of your email address before granting an authenticated voting or administrative session, and to support single-use password recovery.</li>
        <li>To authenticate users, enforce role boundaries and voting-group eligibility, and invalidate older sessions when a password is reset.</li>
        <li>To enforce one ballot per student per election, validate position selection limits, and tabulate aggregate election results.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Where Information Is Disclosed</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Public pages:</strong> Candidate profiles (name, affiliation, platform, and photo) and schedules for non-draft elections are visible to guests and signed-in users. Aggregate vote counts and percentages are disclosed publicly only after an election has been closed by an administrator. Draft elections and draft candidate photos are hidden from non-administrators.</li>
        <li><strong>Student portal:</strong> Signed-in students see open and scheduled elections matching their voting group, their own ballot submission history timestamps, and aggregate results for closed elections.</li>
        <li><strong>Administrator portal &amp; printable reports:</strong> Authorized administrators view registered student account details (to assign voting groups), monitor aggregate ballot counts by election, and generate printable election reports showing aggregate candidate tallies. Neither the admin screens nor printable reports display account-level ballot choices.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Who Can Administer Elections</h2>
    <p>
        Only authenticated, email-verified accounts holding the <code>Admin</code> role can create or manage elections, positions, candidates, candidate photos, student voting groups, and administrator invitations. Administrator accounts can only be created using an authorized bootstrap code (before any administrator exists) or a single-use invitation generated by an existing administrator.
    </p>

    <h2>5. How to Raise a Privacy Request</h2>
    <p>
        Under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173), data subjects may inquire about their personal data or request correction of inaccurate account details (such as name, year level, or voting group). Because this page is institutional draft copy, please direct privacy inquiries or correction requests through ACMCL College Inc.'s designated school administrative office or an active election administrator. Retention, archival, and disposal schedules are governed by ACMCL College Inc. institutional policies.
    </p>
</div>
